ACTUAL LIMITS / FAILURE MODES

• Illustrated top-down sprites rather than complete biomechanics, physiological scaling, fluid dynamics, 3D contact or photorealistic video.
• Mass (kg) labels are toy registry values, not verified estimates. A giant spider at this size violates or stresses ordinary biological constraints; current movement, exoskeleton, respiration, load-bearing, venom potency, and web strength are not solved.
• Body shape is stylistic. Collision geometry, depth/height, terrain occlusion, realistic hearing, vision, learning and social dynamics are minimal or absent.
• Outcome proportions across runs are MODEL OUTPUTS sensitive to arbitrary coefficients—not empirical or historical win probabilities. Independent reference data for mythical encounters cannot exist; for such cases assess only internal consistency/sensitivity and plausible constraints.
• Seeded replay is deterministic in a compatible JS engine, but floating-point, future code changes, or altered time steps can alter trajectories. Pin model version and code hash for scientific reproducibility.
• Current two-agent engine is a slice. A universal system should eventually support any number of heterogeneous actors, neutral bystanders, collectives/swarms, ecology and resource loops, noncombat interactions and emergent diplomacy.

INVARIANTS / TEST ORACLES

I1 Lens isolation: pause; change lenses/split view; numeric state and event ledger remain exactly unchanged.
I2 Branch accountability: edit a causal setting and log a new parameter baseline; replay older snapshots with the old settings.
I3 Seed determinism: identical code, seed, fixed dt and settings yield identical final state.
I4 Grounding: visual/literary intensity does not upgrade evidence grade.
I5 Agency: allow avoidance/retreat, not merely preordained attacks; role, fear, energy and sensory limits may matter.
I6 Nonoverfit: test models with withheld real observations; report uncertainties and regime boundaries.
I7 Adaptive resolution: increase representation/physics/agent detail only when it improves causal usefulness, scientific testability or artistic experience.
I8 Provenance: export assumptions, parameter values, seeds, event history, scenario class and fidelity.
I9 Multi-world comparison: control initial state and random seeds when comparing terrain or parameter interventions.
I10 Ethics: never require real animal violence; simulations are synthetic thought experiments.

